  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Zambia 2026 &#x2013; Urban WASH Emergency Officer</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia is increasingly vulnerable to climate-related hazards such as floods and disease outbreaks that threaten water security, public health, and infrastructure. Heavy rainfall on 29&#x2013;30 December 2025 caused severe flooding in Lundazi District, Eastern Province, collapsing the Lundazi Dam wall, washing away bridges, submerging the water treatment plant, and destroying hundreds of homes. Around 50 households were completely submerged, 250 collapsed, and roughly 50,000 people were affected, with numbers expected to rise. The flooding shut down the Eastern Water and Sanitation Company&#x2019;s treatment plant, halting water supply and damaging critical equipment, while also heightening risks of disease outbreaks like cholera. UNICEF is supporting national and local authorities to strengthen emergency preparedness, coordination, and resilience, and is seeking a WASH Emergency Specialist with flood-response and urban water-utility experience to support a coordinated and effective response in Lundazi.</narrative>
  </description>
